<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Poděbrady</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lords of Kunštát and Poděbrady</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Poděbrady were a Bohemian noble family named after their castle at Poděbrady on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elbe">Elbe</a>, whose most famous member was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-of-podebrady">George of Poděbrady</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-of-bohemia">King of Bohemia</a> from 1458 to 1471. His sons became dukes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ziebice">Münsterberg</a> (Ziębice) and held Silesian duchies including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olesnica">Oleśnica</a> and, for a time, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/opava">Opava</a>. The family's Münsterberg-Oels line adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lutheranism">Lutheranism</a> and died out in the male line in 1647.</p></div>
